    "description": "The billing platform stores CustomerProfile objects in CustomerDirectory. A profile currently contains a mutable email address, postal address, plan name, and legacy account number. Customers may change all of these attributes, while invoices, subscriptions, audit entries, and cached account references must continue to point to the same person. Conversely, two different customers can share an email address or display name, so those attributes cannot establish sameness. The legacy account number is being replaced by a new identifier format, but old invoice links must remain valid during the migration. CustomerDirectory lookups need to distinguish identity from current attribute values, and equality checks must not report one customer as another after an address or plan change. The model must also retain enough lifecycle information to tell whether a profile is active, suspended, or closed without relying on its mutable descriptive fields.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose how a customer's persistent identity and sameness are represented so that attribute and storage changes do not break existing references, while shared attributes do not merge distinct customers.",
    "notes": "entity primary: stable customer identity must survive attribute, format, and storage changes while shared attributes must not merge distinct customers; aggregate is the cluster-boundary near-miss."
